Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:10:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: regenerate the getblockstats fixture

rpc_getblockstats replays a stored chain and compares getblockstats
output with stored values. Since v2/034 regenerated the fixture,
consensus code has changed in ways that alter block contents and state
roots (later V2 fixups on this branch among them). The node now
rejected stored block 103 with bad-blk-stateroot, so the replay stopped
at height 102 and the test failed with "Target block height 103 after
current tip 102".

The fixture is regenerated with the test's own --gen-test-data mode.
Only blocks 102 and 103 and the two block hashes in the expected stats
change; every statistic (fees, fee rates, sizes, input and output
counts) is identical, so the test still checks the same accounting.
The regenerated fixture replays on a fresh node and the test passes.

Tier: V2 (fixup to v2/034)
---
 test/functional/data/rpc_getblockstats.json | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/test/functional/data/rpc_getblockstats.json b/test/functional/data/rpc_getblockstats.json
index f5078ee984..41c8bc9625 100644
--- a/test/functional/data/rpc_getblockstats.json
+++ b/test/functional/data/rpc_getblockstats.json
@@ -102,8 +102,8 @@
     "",
